{
 "id": "fx-sends",
 "version": "1.1",
 "title": "FX SENDS",
 "category": "Effect",
 "author": "hugz202 (AE-analog-rytm-mods); MKII port: Iced-Cream",
 "license": "MIT",
 "description": "A chorus as one more send effect, with the Analog Four chorus's controls. On a drum track, press AMP a second time for the SEND page: CHR, the track's send to a stereo chorus (saved with the sound, in core-ar2's mod storage). On the FX track, press DELAY a second time for the CHORUS page: the chorus's settings PRE, SPD, DEP, WID, FDB, HPF and the return's level VOL, saved with the kit (core-ar2 kit fields, the MK1's defaults in a new kit). The chorus runs on the ColdFire in the audio interrupt after the stock delay and reverb, on the voices the codec captured: two interpolated taps on one line, a one-pole high-pass on its input, the taps' average fed back. Its return joins the delay and reverb returns' PRE words (into the analog distortion and compressor) and follows the FX track's level, as the stock returns do. Nothing runs while no track sends. From 1.1 all eight are lockable parameters (core-ar2 0.10): p-locked with a trig held, locked in scenes and performances, on MIDI as NRPNs; CHR is an LFO, velocity and aftertouch destination on its track, the chorus settings FX LFO destinations on the FX track. The audio reads each as stock would play it. Its knobs are the hidden CY TEST machine's parameter records, renamed. Needs core-ar2 0.10 (its page tables, lockable parameters, 14 bits of sound storage and 56 of the kit's 64), so it cannot share a build with both voice-dac and lfo-rnd, or with duck 1.1. Port of AE-analog-rytm-mods 0010-fx-sends (Analog Rytm MK1).",
 "device": "analog-rytm-mk2",
 "os": "1.74",
